From e802f9e86dcb6d33430580fda3cee9ce43ed7169 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kamal Bura <burakamal13@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 16:04:25 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] mediatek: filogic: add JioRouter AX6000 JIDU6801 to JIDU6J01
 target

The JioRouter AX6000 JIDU6801 is a dual-band Wi-Fi 6 router based on the
MediaTek MT7986A (Filogic 830) SoC. It shares the identical hardware
platform with the other JioRouter AX6000 family variants (JIDU6201,
JIDU6401, JIDU6601, JIDU6701) supported by jiorouter_ax6000-jidu6j01.

Hardware:
- SoC: MediaTek MT7986A (4x ARM Cortex-A53 @ 2.0 GHz)
- RAM: 512 MiB DDR4
- Flash: 256 MiB SPI-NAND (Winbond W25N02KV, MediaTek NMBM)
- Ethernet: 5x 10/100/1000 Mbps Gigabit ports (1 WAN + 4 LAN)
  * Switch: MediaTek MT7531AE DSA
  * Port 0: 1 Gbps WAN (internal MT7531 PHY)
  * Ports 1-4: 1 Gbps LAN (internal MT7531 PHYs)
  * Port 6: 2.5 Gbps SGMII CPU link to gmac0 (2500Base-X)
- Wireless: MediaTek MT7976C DBDC, 4x4 2.4 GHz + 4x4 5 GHz (AX6000)
- LEDs: 3x GPIO-controlled (Red GPIO 12, Green GPIO 13, Blue GPIO 14)
- Button: 1x Reset (GPIO 9)
- USB: 1x USB 3.0 Type-A host
- UART: 115200 8N1 (3.3V TTL header)
- Power: 12V DC, 2.5A (barrel jack, 5.5mm/2.1mm center-positive)

MAC address layout:
- WAN / Label: MFG MTD partition, offset 0x00 (6 bytes binary)
- LAN: WAN + 1
- 2.4 GHz: WAN + 2
- 5 GHz: WAN + 3

Flashing instructions:
1. Connect a 3.3V USB-to-UART adapter to the serial header (115200 8N1).
2. Retrieve U-Boot credentials from the MFG partition (root access on stock
   OS, or SPI-NAND dump).
3. Power on the router and interrupt boot in the serial console using the
   extracted credentials.
4. Set up TFTP server on host PC (192.168.1.2) and boot initramfs image:
     setenv ipaddr 192.168.1.1
     setenv serverip 192.168.1.2
     tftpboot 0x46000000 openwrt-mediatek-filogic-jiorouter_ax6000-jidu6j01-initramfs-kernel.bin
     fdt addr $(fdtcontroladdr)
     fdt rm /signature
     bootm
5. Once booted into OpenWrt initramfs, flash the sysupgrade image:
     sysupgrade -n /tmp/openwrt-mediatek-filogic-jiorouter_ax6000-jidu6j01-squashfs-sysupgrade.bin

The board is identical in device tree and hardware architecture to the
existing jidu6j01 image, so add JIDU6801 as DEVICE_ALT4_VARIANT under
jiorouter_ax6000-jidu6j01. The base MAC address is stored at offset 0x00
binary in the MFG partition, matching the default MFG fallback.

Signed-off-by: Kamal Bura <burakamal13@gmail.com>
---
 target/linux/mediatek/image/filogic.mk | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/target/linux/mediatek/image/filogic.mk b/target/linux/mediatek/image/filogic.mk
index d07abed..4e45292 100644
--- a/target/linux/mediatek/image/filogic.mk
+++ b/target/linux/mediatek/image/filogic.mk
@@ -2346,6 +2346,9 @@ define Device/jiorouter_ax6000-jidu6j01
   DEVICE_ALT3_VENDOR := JioRouter
   DEVICE_ALT3_MODEL := AX6000
   DEVICE_ALT3_VARIANT := JIDU6701
+  DEVICE_ALT4_VENDOR := JioRouter
+  DEVICE_ALT4_MODEL := AX6000
+  DEVICE_ALT4_VARIANT := JIDU6801
   DEVICE_DTS := mt7986a-jiorouter-ax6000-jidu6j01
   DEVICE_DTS_DIR := ../dts
   DEVICE_PACKAGES := kmod-usb3 kmod-mt7915e kmod-mt7986-firmware mt7986-wo-firmware
-- 
